    "architects": "Tremend Architecture Studio",
    "year": "2023",
    "materials_detail": "Stainless steel latticed mushroom-shaped structural pillars and canopy; glass; energy-efficient LED lighting; greywater system for rainwater capture used in irrigation and landscaping",
    "summary_en": "The Metropolitan Station in Lublin, Poland, completed in 2023 by Tremend Architecture Studio, is the centerpiece of the city's Integrated Transportation Hub. Conceived as a contemporary pavilion, the station is defined by its distinctive mushroom-shaped columns of latticed steel that simultaneously serve structural and decorative roles, supporting a sweeping canopy clad in stainless steel and glass. The project aims to revitalize the surrounding railway station district and create a new urban fabric. Sustainability measures include energy-efficient LED lighting and a greywater system that captures rainfall for irrigation and landscaping.",
