    "materials_detail": "Brick walls based on traditional stretcher bond with gray-scale gradation; dark blue shale roof tiles; H-shaped steel beams with variable sections; timber components fabricated via digital wood fabrication; glass; robotically prefabricated brick units",
    "summary_en": "The Inkstone House OCT Linpan Cultural Center, completed in 2018 by Archi-Union Architects, is a 2,200 m² cultural complex situated in the rural Linpan landscape of Anren, Sichuan. The design draws inspiration from the traditional Chinese inkstone and the historic Western Sichuan Linpan settlement typology. Driven by digital design and fabrication technology, the project employed robotic Digital Brick Construction with over 400 prefabricated brick units and digitally fabricated timber elements. The facade features traditional stretcher-bond brickwork with a gray-scale gradient, while the roof is clad in dark blue shale tiles.",
